  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, there is zero evidence about which design choices matter. The most informative first step is to establish a simple, fast baseline that anchors all future comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest configuration in the space: it uses a non-learned linear encoder (PCA), avoids aggregation and fusion complexity, and isolates the contribution of RNA data alone. This gives us (1) a performance floor, (2) a reference to judge whether more complex encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, or multimodal fusion actually add value, and (3) a fast-to-run experiment that conserves budget for later, more targeted comparisons. Establishing this baseline before testing any image-only or multimodal variant ensures we can attribute performance gains to specific design decisions rather than confounding multiple factors."
